WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.033
-Our next guest is a talented
actor who you can see in

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.501
the new series "The Afterparty,"

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.501
which premieres this Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.033
Please welcome Dave Franco!

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.667
That's what I'm talking about.
Yes!

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.167
Dave, thank you
for being here, buddy.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.100
I really appreciate this.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.701
-Of course.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.834
-Last time you were here,

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:25.601
we talked about your cats.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:29.601
So I should just ask, just to be
polite, how are your cats?

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:30.767
-Yeah, that checks out.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:34.834
I actually did another interview
recently where

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.968
the journalist asked,
"What defines you?

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.901
You know, What do most people
associate you with?"

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.367
And I was like, "Wow,
that's a really good question."

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:45.467
And all of my castmates chimed
in, and they were like, "Cats."

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:49.033
And I was like, "Wow,
I guess that is sadly true."

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.167
But for whatever reason,
at some point,

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.033
being obsessed with cats became,

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.434
like, a quirky character trait.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:59.100
Like, why is loving cats
not the norm?

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.267
-Wow. I mean, do you really --

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.868
It is, I mean, kind of the norm.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.033
I mean, some people
are dog people, I guess,

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:07.067
but some people are --
You know, I --

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.167
-Everyone's dog people.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.000
If you look at
all popular culture,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.968
anytime there's a cat onscreen,
they're the bad guy.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.067
What's up with that?

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.868
And so, like,
within our household,

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.834
we treat our two cats
like little gods.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.601
And we've actually gotten to
the point where

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:23.501
we start having back-and-forth
conversations with them.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.834
We are -- We have
turned into those people.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:29.367
-Wow. We actually have
a video of

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.167
Dave Franco in conversation
with his cat, Otis.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.067
This is real. Take a look.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.801
-Odie.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.834
[ Cat meows ]

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.000
Otis.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.033
[ Cat meows ]

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.434
O-Boy.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.000
[ Cat meows ]

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.501
-Wow! I've never seen anyone
do that in my life.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:54.067
-Hey, I've heard
all this stuff about

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.000
Chris Evans' dog being famous.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.834
I'm just trying to get my boy
Otis up there with him.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.200
-That's what
I'm talking about, Otis.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.501
Let's get Otis a movie.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:03.934
Let's get Otis a voiceover.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.834
At least a voiceover
in a cartoon.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.067
-Absolutely.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.100
-I want to talk about
"The Afterparty."

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.734
It premieres this Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.234
Man, is it funny.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.167
And it's from
the same team that did

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.267
"21 Jump Street"
and the "Lego" movies.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.400
If you guys saw any of
the "Lego" movies.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.400
-Yeah.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.400
-They're brilliant.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.000
It is such a -- They're such

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.133
great writers, producers,
directors.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:28.901
But can you set up what
"The Afterparty" is all about?

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:34.634
-Yes, so, it's a murder mystery
set at a high-school reunion,

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.400
where each episode is told from

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.367
a different character's
point of view.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.501
And the character's personality

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.834
actually informs
the genre of each episode.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:47.934
So, like, the jocks episode
is shot like an action movie,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.567
and the art-students episode
is actually animated.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:51.734
And so on and so on.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:54.033
So it's, like,
a very, very unique concept.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:58.467
-You play a famous
pop singer named Xavier.

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.100
-Correct.
-Great name, by the way.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.968
And you have a great look.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.000
I guess we do have
a picture of it.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.901
Here's Xavier here.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.701
Yeah. Now, Xavier had to --

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.501
You had to record some
original pop songs.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:15.100
Do you get nervous when
you have to sing or no,

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.834
you're like, "Oh, I can do it"?

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:20.434
-No, I'm not very proficient
when it comes to singing.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.033
This was my first time,
like, doing it "professionally,"

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.734
and it was very scary.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.734
I mean, not just the singing,
but the actual songs.

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:31.133
You know, titles like
"X Marks the G-Spot"

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.467
and "Do Wet."

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:34.801
It's "D-O Wet,"

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:38.300
and it's everything the
character likes doing while wet.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:41.400
And so you can imagine
the explicit lyrics

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.501
that come with all of that.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:45.367
-Yeah, I can. Yeah, I can.

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:49.133
-And my vocal coach,
Fiora Cutler --

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:52.334
she is just the
sweetest person in the world.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:54.667
And, so, just,
you know, imagining me

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.234
earnestly trying to sing those
graphic lyrics to her,

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:00.267
we were both
very, very embarrassed for me.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.667
But we have now gotten to
the point where

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:07.534
we have recorded four songs and
we have a full E.P. coming out.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:10.567
And we shot
a music video, as well.

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:12.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, gosh.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.167
Okay. Look for --

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:18.567
Is "X Marks"
the first one coming up?

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:20.267
-Oh, "X Marks the G-Spot."

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.234
Yeah, that's the hit single,
I think,

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:23.901
but we got "Do Wet."

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:27.267
We got "I'mma Live Forever"
and we got "Just Like You"...

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.000
-Alright, yeah.
-...yeah, coming out soon.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.133
-Yeah, "Do Wet."

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.467
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.234
-I do want to give away
a spoiler, by the way.

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:38.567
But -- Well, I'm allowed to,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.734
because we asked you before if
we could talk about this,

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:43.901
because your character,
supposedly, is in a --

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:45.534
was in a Hall &amp; Oates biopic.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:47.000
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.968
-And so they show a scene from
that -- scenes from that.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:53.234
And it's you and Channing Tatum
as Hall &amp; Oates.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:56.167
-Yeah.

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.133
-Was --
[ Applause ]

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:03.367
People want to see this.
-Yeah.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:07.300
-Apparently, what I heard
is that when you were doing it,

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.267
it just turned out to be
so much fun,

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.834
everything was working that
you wanted to kept shooting

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:15.133
and you almost recorded
like four hours of this bit.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:18.634
-Yeah. So, on the page,
it was probably like maybe

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:20.701
three or four lines
back and forth,

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:23.267
and we ended up filming for
like three or four hours.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.434
We just couldn't stop riffing
on Hall &amp; Oates.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:30.667
And, you know, there's probably
like a 30-minute cut out there

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.968
of me and Channing just kind of
going back and forth,

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.534
arguing about who gets to
have the mustache,

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.033
because you can't have
a two-man band and two 'staches.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.567
You've got to pick one.
-That's correct. That's correct.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.300
-Yeah. Everyone knows the rules.
-Oates is the guy.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.234
Of course. Yeah, John Oates.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.167
You brought us
an exclusive clip.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:49.567
Here's Dave Franco and
Channing Tatum

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:52.567
as Hall &amp; Oates
in "The Afterparty."

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:54.133
Take a look at this.

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:55.567
-Aah!

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.667
You see -- that -- that right
there is what we need.

00:05:57.667 --> 00:06:00.234
-A broken record?
-No, a smash hit!

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:03.534
This city will
put you in its mouth,

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:05.067
bite you up, and spit you out.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:06.734
It's a -- It's an eater of men.

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:08.968
♪♪

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:12.801
-Wait. What did you just say?

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:15.200
Grab your ax.
It's chart-breaking time!

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.667
-Let's break them charts.
Come on, let's see.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.701
-Okay, you go high.
I'll go the same high.

00:06:18.701 --> 00:06:20.567
-Okay.
-And a one and...

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:24.267
-Yeah. And that's how they
wrote "Maneater."

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:26.434
Of course, that's exactly how.

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:27.734
Dave Franco, everybody.
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:32.000
-"The Afterparty" premieres
this Friday on Apple TV+.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.100
It is super-funny,
super-well-done.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.968
Good to see you.
Best to Alison, buddy.

